<h1>Capture Dynamic Points</h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Capture Dynamic Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command captures stream of points from the first time switch '</span>B' <span lang="EN-GB">is depressed until the second time it is depressed. Several streams of points may be captured by repeatedly pausing/restarting with the '</span>B' <span lang="EN-GB">button. Depressing switch '</span>A' <span lang="EN-GB">terminates dynamic point capture. This command is normally used to capture ball probe points on the object’s bodylines.</span> This command is accessible from <span class="Path">System &gt; Performance Check Utilities &gt; Capture &gt; Dynamic Points</span>. It is also accessible from <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'Capture dynamic points'</b></span> button on the toolbar.</p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span><span><i style="font-weight:bold;">Capture dynamic points'</i></span> <span lang="EN-GB">is not selected, hold down the left mouse button on the current selection for a second to show up the drop-down toolbar. Select '</span><i style="font-style:normal;">Capture dynamic points'</i> <span lang="EN-GB">button from there.</span></p>
<p><img src="Capture_files/capture_dynamic_points.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
